course: dictionary
lesson: 15194
title: Sedum: a plant that stores water
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words name things you may never have seen. You can still work out a lot from the words around them. «The sedum on the wall had thick, fleshy leaves full of water.» Thick leaves full of water tell you that sedum is a plant that stores water.
explain: Clues can also come from other words in the sentence. Sedum grows on rocks, walls and roofs, and it has star-shaped flowers. «Bees buzzed around the sedum flowers all afternoon.» Bees like flowers, so sedum must be a plant with flowers that bees visit.
explain: Always check your meaning. Swap it into the sentence in place of the hard word. «The sedum on the wall was a small plant that stores water» still makes sense, so your meaning is probably right.
fact: A sedum is a small plant with thick, fleshy leaves that store water.
fact: Sedum is also called stonecrop.
fact: Many sedums have star-shaped flowers and grow on rocks, walls and roofs.
fact: «Green roofs» are often covered in sedum, because it needs little soil and water.
fact: Bees and butterflies love the flowers of sedum.
exercise: «The sedum on the wall had thick, fleshy leaves full of water.» What is a sedum? | A tall tree with a thick trunk | A kind of stone used to build walls | *A small plant that stores water | A type of small bird
exercise: «Bees buzzed around the sedum flowers all afternoon.» Which insects love sedum flowers? | *Bees and butterflies | Snakes and spiders | Fish and frogs | Dogs and cats
exercise: Another name for sedum is stonecrop. Which word is another name for sedum? | Starfish | Stone wall | *Stonecrop | Seaweed
test: «Green roofs are often covered in sedum because it needs little soil and water.» Why are green roofs often covered in sedum? | It is very tall and strong | *It needs little soil and water | It needs lots of soil and water | It only grows in the sea
test: Where does sedum often grow? | Inside a fridge | Deep in a cave | *On rocks, walls and roofs | Under the sea
exam: What does the word sedum name? | A tall tree with a thick trunk | A large rock by the sea | *A small plant with thick leaves that stores water | A kind of bird that lives on roofs
